// EXPECTED: syntax error(s). Line 5 is missing the terminating semicolon
// after the assignment, which violates <assignment> ::= IDENTIFIER "="
// <expr> ";". A second, independent violation on line 9 (missing closing
// parenthesis on the while condition) is included deliberately to verify
// the parser's error recovery continues past the first error rather than
// halting silently after just one diagnostic.

int x;
int y;
x = 5
y = 10;

while (x > 0 {
    x = x - 1;
}

print y;
